Subject: [PATCH] webapp: fix RCE — parse Dash callback id with json.loads instead of eval

The `layout_filter` callback parsed the triggered component id with `eval()`. The triggered
`prop_id` comes from the client-supplied `changedPropIds` of the `/_dash-update-component`
request, so this allowed unauthenticated remote code execution on the host running the
dashboard. Dash serialises pattern-matching ids as JSON, so `json.loads` is a
behaviour-preserving, safe replacement (returns the same {"index": ...} dict; rejects
non-JSON payloads with JSONDecodeError).

--- a/shapash/webapp/smart_app.py
+++ b/shapash/webapp/smart_app.py
@@ -3,6 +3,7 @@
 """
 
 import copy
+import json
 import random
 import re
 from math import isfinite, log10
@@ -2994,7 +2995,7 @@
                 return [html.Div(id={"type": "bloc_div", "index": 0}, children=[])]
             # Removal of an existing filter
             else:
-                filter_id_to_remove = eval(button_id)["index"]
+                filter_id_to_remove = json.loads(button_id)["index"]
                 return [gr for gr in currents_filters if gr["props"]["id"]["index"] != filter_id_to_remove]
 
         @app.callback(
